// The `i32` an `x as% i32` yields, delivered everywhere. `as%` is the wrap cast — DECISIONS.md
// §"`as%` is the wrap cast, the fourth member of the `as` family" — so unlike the exact three
// it has no null, no trap and no propagation: the result is an ordinary `i32` and every
// position that takes an `i32` must take this one.
//
// The operand is an `i64` past the i32 range, so a cell that lost the wrap prints a different
// number rather than the same one by luck: 5000000123 wraps to 705032827, and the PROOF adds.
//
// The second instance is the `u8` domain, whose lowering is the wrap plus a byte mask — the
// same delivery matrix, a different tail instruction.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
function wide(): i64 { return 5000000123 }
function alsoWide(): i64 { return 1000 }
// @@VALUE@@
wide() as% i32
// @@TYPE@@
i32
// @@PROOF@@
print(v + 1)
// @@WANT@@
705032828
// @@TEST@@
v > 100
// @@HIT@@
print(v + 1)
// @@MISS@@
print(0)
// @@VALUE2@@
alsoWide() as% u8
// @@TYPE2@@
i32
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v + 1)
// @@WANT2@@
233
